# NovaLabs

Interactive astronomy lab platform for education.

[![Python 3.11+](https://img.shields.io/badge/python-3.11+-blue.svg)](https://www.python.org/downloads/)
[![License: AGPL v3](https://img.shields.io/badge/License-AGPL_v3-blue.svg)](https://www.gnu.org/licenses/agpl-3.0)

## Overview

NovaLabs is a modular platform for creating and delivering interactive astronomy laboratory exercises. It provides:

- **Structured lab framework** - Briefings, quizzes, exercises with predictions/observations/conclusions
- **Progress tracking** - Track student progress, time spent, and grades
- **Flexible grading** - Auto-graded quizzes + instructor-graded exercises
- **Interactive visualizations** - Integration with Stellarium and other tools

## Architecture

```
novalabs/
├── common/          # Shared utilities (database, config)
├── core/            # Lab framework (models, managers, UI base classes)
├── hub/             # Central hub (authentication, API, admin)
├── labs/            # Individual lab implementations
│   └── celestial_sphere/
│       └── content/     # TOML + Markdown content files
└── scripts/         # CLI tools
```

### Layer Overview

| Layer | Purpose | Key Components |
|-------|---------|----------------|
| **common** | Shared infrastructure | Database connection, configuration |
| **core** | Lab framework | Models, content loading, managers, UI base classes |
| **hub** | Central services | Authentication, REST API, admin interface |
| **labs** | Lab implementations | Content files, custom UI components |

### Data Flow

```
┌─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────┐
│                         Lab Flow                                │
├─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────┤
│                                                                 │
│  ┌──────────────┐    ┌──────────────┐    ┌──────────────┐      │
│  │   Briefing   │───▶│   Pre-Quiz   │───▶│  Exercises   │      │
│  │   (read)     │    │   (8/10)     │    │   (1-N)      │      │
│  └──────────────┘    └──────────────┘    └──────────────┘      │
│                                                 │               │
│                                                 ▼               │
│                                          ┌──────────────┐      │
│                                          │  Post-Quiz   │      │
│                                          │   (8/10)     │      │
│                                          └──────────────┘      │
│                                                 │               │
│                                                 ▼               │
│                                          ┌──────────────┐      │
│                                          │   Grading    │      │
│                                          │ (instructor) │      │
│                                          └──────────────┘      │
└─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────┘
```

## Installation

```bash
# Clone the repository
git clone https://github.com/aprsa/novalabs.git
cd novalabs

# Install with development dependencies
pip install -e ".[dev]"

# Initialize the database
novalabs-initdb

# Create an admin user
novalabs-createadmin --email admin@example.com

# Load lab content
novalabs-loadlabs
```

## Quick Start

### 1. Initialize Database

```bash
novalabs-initdb --verbose
```

### 2. Create Users

```bash
# Create admin
novalabs-createadmin --email admin@villanova.edu --generate-password

# Create students
novalabs-createuser --email student@villanova.edu --first-name Jane --last-name Doe --role student
```

### 3. Load Lab Content

```bash
# Load all labs
novalabs-loadlabs

# Load specific lab
novalabs-loadlabs --lab celestial_sphere

# Validate without loading
novalabs-loadlabs --validate-only
```

### 4. Start the Hub

```bash
novalabs-hub
```

## Lab Content Structure

Labs are defined using TOML configuration files and Markdown content:

```
labs/celestial_sphere/
├── __init__.py
├── lab.py                  # Python code (UI customization)
└── content/
    ├── lab.toml            # Lab metadata
    ├── briefing.md         # Mission briefing
    ├── pre_quiz.toml       # Pre-lab quiz questions
    ├── post_quiz.toml      # Post-lab quiz questions
    └── exercises/
        └── 01_polaris_latitude/
            ├── exercise.toml
            ├── instructions.md
            ├── prediction.md
            └── conclusion.md
```

### lab.toml

```toml
[lab]
slug = "celestial_sphere"
title = "The Celestial Sphere"
description = "Understand Earth's rotation and revolution"
passing_score = 8

[briefing]
file = "briefing.md"

[pre_quiz]
file = "pre_quiz.toml"

[post_quiz]
file = "post_quiz.toml"

[[exercises]]
dir = "01_polaris_latitude"
max_points = 20

[[exercises]]
dir = "02_day_night_duration"
max_points = 20
```

### pre_quiz.toml

```toml
[quiz]
instructions = "Answer based on the Mission Briefing."

[[questions]]
text = "What causes the apparent daily motion of stars?"
options = [
    "Earth's rotation on its axis",
    "Earth's revolution around the Sun",
    "The Moon's gravitational pull",
    "Stars actually moving through space"
]
correct = 0
```

### exercise.toml

```toml
[exercise]
number = 1
title = "Polaris and Latitude"
objective = "Discover the relationship between latitude and Polaris altitude"

[files]
instructions_file = "instructions.md"
prediction_file = "prediction.md"
conclusion_file = "conclusion.md"

[stellarium]
latitude = 40.0
longitude = -75.0
look_at = "NAME Polaris"

[[tasks]]
number = 1
type = "data_entry"
prompt = "Record the altitude of Polaris at each latitude:"

[[tasks.columns]]
name = "Latitude"
unit = "°"
editable = false
values = [0, 20, 40, 60, 90]

[[tasks.columns]]
name = "Polaris Altitude"
unit = "°"
editable = true

[[tasks]]
number = 2
type = "short_answer"
prompt = "What pattern do you notice?"
```

## Grading System

### Quiz Scoring

Points per correct answer decrease with each attempt:
- 1st attempt: 1.0 point per correct answer
- 2nd attempt: 0.5 points per correct answer
- 3rd+ attempt: 0.25 points per correct answer

**Correct answers carry over** between attempts. Example:
- Attempt 1: 6 correct → 6.0 points
- Attempt 2: 3 more correct → 1.5 points
- Total: 7.5 points (9 correct answers)

### Total Grade Calculation

```
Lab Grade = Pre-Quiz Points + Exercise Points + Post-Quiz Points

Example:
- Pre-quiz: 8.5 / 10 points
- Exercises: 85 / 100 points (5 × 20, instructor graded)
- Post-quiz: 9.0 / 10 points
- Total: 102.5 / 120 points (85.4%)
```

## CLI Tools

| Command | Description |
|---------|-------------|
| `novalabs-initdb` | Initialize database tables |
| `novalabs-createadmin` | Create an admin user |
| `novalabs-createuser` | Create a regular user |
| `novalabs-loadlabs` | Load lab content into database |
| `novalabs-hub` | Start the hub server |
| `novalabs-shell` | Interactive Python shell with NovaLabs context |

## Development

### Running Tests

```bash
# Run all tests
pytest

# Run core tests only
pytest tests/core/

# With coverage
pytest --cov=novalabs --cov-report=html
```

### Interactive Shell

```bash
novalabs-shell
```

This provides a Python REPL with all models and managers pre-imported:

```python
>>> users = session.exec(select(User)).all()
>>> labs = session.exec(select(Lab)).all()
>>> manager = QuizManager(session, user_id=1, lab_id=1)
```

### Code Style

```bash
# Format code
black novalabs/

# Lint
ruff check novalabs/

# Type checking
mypy novalabs/
```

## Core Components

### Models (`novalabs.core.models`)

| Model | Description |
|-------|-------------|
| `Lab` | Lab metadata and configuration |
| `Question` | Quiz questions (pre and post) |
| `Exercise` | Exercise definitions |
| `ExerciseTask` | Individual tasks within exercises |
| `StudentLabProgress` | Overall progress per student per lab |
| `StudentQuizAttempt` | Quiz attempt history |
| `StudentExerciseResponse` | Exercise predictions/conclusions |
| `StudentTaskResponse` | Individual task responses |
| `StudentTimeTracking` | Time spent per segment |

### Managers (`novalabs.core.managers`)

| Manager | Purpose |
|---------|---------|
| `QuizManager` | Quiz logic, scoring, attempt tracking |
| `ExerciseManager` | Exercise flow, response saving, submission |
| `ProgressManager` | Overall progress, grading, status transitions |
| `TimeTracker` | Time tracking per segment |

### Content Loading (`novalabs.core.content`)

| Function | Description |
|----------|-------------|
| `discover_labs()` | Find valid labs in a directory |
| `validate_lab_structure()` | Validate lab content structure |
| `load_lab_content()` | Load TOML/MD into database |

## Configuration

Configuration is loaded from `config.toml` with environment variable overrides:

```toml
[database]
url = "sqlite:///novalabs.db"

[labs]
directory = "./labs"

debug = false
```

Environment variables:
- `NOVALABS_CONFIG` - Path to config file
- `NOVALABS_DATABASE_URL` - Database URL override
- `NOVALABS_LABS_DIR` - Labs directory override
- `NOVALABS_DEBUG` - Enable debug mode

